ok - malformed JSON never reaches sm-verify
ok - an oversize request is refused unread
ok - symlinks and special files in the spool are never read
ok - only <digits>.json names are processed
ok - unknown verbs, extra keys and hostile tab names are rejected
ok - steps outside the allowlist are rejected
ok - a worker cannot supply YAML, a header or an appId
ok - inputText, Enter and the other forbidden commands are rejected
ok - denylisted selectors are rejected, including tab names and punctuation variants
ok - allowed steps become a host-generated flow with literal selectors
ok - evidence is limited to real PNG files and text is control-stripped
ok - results are atomic, complete and answered once
ok - a failing sm-verify is reported faithfully
ok - a rename or symlink swap during the copy cannot change what runs
ok - no worker-supplied path or string reaches the sm-verify invocation
ok - the pinned sm-verify must be a host-owned file matching its digest
ok - a modified sm-verify no longer runs
ok - status is answered by the broker without sm-verify or the lease
ok - a second client is queued and gets the emulator after the first lets go
ok - waiters are served first come first served
ok - an idle lease expires with a forced down
ok - requests keep the lease alive
ok - teardown while holding the lease forces the emulator down and frees it
ok - stop recovers an emulator left up by a killed broker
ok - removing the sandbox ends the lease with a forced down
ok - exactly one bundle file is served, everything else is a plain 404
ok - a down that exits nonzero still ends the lease
ok - the bundle must be one regular file
ok - every request, verdict and digest is appended to the host audit log
ok - without the token the sandbox config has no verification broker
ok - iOS requests are refused unless config/sbx-verify names an iOS host
ok - iOS requests go through the same validator, allowlists and denylist
ok - an iOS verb runs the pinned command on the Mac, never with the Apple account
ok - iOS flows are generated on the host and evidence is checked like Android's
ok - evidence from the Mac keeps the count, size, name and PNG limits
ok - the remote command quotes every word once and refuses control bytes
ok - Mac paths are absolute, plain and free of dot-dot segments
ok - the iOS config keys are validated and need each other
ok - a Mac command that does not match its pin is never run
ok - SSH failures are typed errors and never fall back to a local run
ok - each phase has its own time limit and a hung ssh cannot hold the broker
ok - iOS has its own lease, queue and status, apart from Android
ok - teardown while holding the iOS lease sends down and frees it
ok - a killed broker, a vanished sandbox and an idle lease all send down to the Mac
ok - the audit log says which platform each request used
# all fm-sbx-verify-broker tests passed
